#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley is a vocabulary trainer. It helps you to memorize your vocabulary, "
"for example when you are trying to learn a foreign language. You can create "
"your own vocabulary collections with the words you need or select from a "
"great variety of available <ulink url=\"http://userbase.kde.org/"
"Parley#Vocabulary_Collections\">Vocabulary Collections</ulink>. There you "
"can find collections containing language vocabulary and also anatomy, music, "
"geography, chemistry or exam preparation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley is very flexible and uses the <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/Flashcard\">flash card learning approach</ulink>. It automatically "
"keeps track of your learning progress. With Parley you can arrange your "
"vocabulary as you wish, you create your own lessons as needed. But unlike "
"real flash cards you can use different learning methods with Parley."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Flashcards contain expressions on the front side and their translation on "
"the back. You start with a pile of cards. If you know the translation on a "
"card, you can put it into a second pile of cards. If you did not remember "
"it, you keep it in the first one to try again later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley's main focus is not to teach you grammar. However, there are some "
"exercise forms which may help you in this matter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley consists of two big parts: <link linkend=\"practice\">Vocabulary "
"Practice</link> and <link linkend=\"vocabulary-editing\">an Editor for "
"Vocabulary Collections</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this manual the term <emphasis>Vocabulary Collection</emphasis> refers to "
"a file that contains lessons and the vocabulary in the lessons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Both, the Editor and the Practice can be reached from the <link linkend="
"\"start-page\">Start Page</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <link linkend=\"practice\">Practice</link> consists of three parts: "
"first the <link linkend=\"practice-setup\">Practice Setup</link> where you "
"choose what to practice. From there you start the actual <link linkend="
"\"practice\">Practice</link> and when you are done, you get a <link linkend="
"\"summary-after-practice\">Summary</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Like in all applications try to use the right-click if you explore features "
"and functionality in Parley. The right-click displays a <quote>context menu</"
"quote> that shows what you can do with your present situation. Try right-"
"clicking lessons and words to find some options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you first launch Parley the <guilabel>Start Page</guilabel> welcomes "
"you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At first the <guilabel>Start Page</guilabel> is empty, once you opened some "
"vocabulary collections, it shows you the ones you worked with most recently."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A vocabulary collection is a file that contains words and their translations "
"into other languages or other pairs of words and sentences that you want to "
"memorize. The words are organized in lessons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To <emphasis>start practicing</emphasis>, click one of the vocabulary "
"collections in the list. You are taken to the <link linkend=\"practice-setup"
"\">practice setup</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that a small <guilabel>Editor Icon</guilabel> appears to the right of "
"the document name when you move the mouse over it. The <guilabel>Editor "
"Icon</guilabel> lets you open the collection in the editor instead of "
"practice mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To <link linkend=\"vocabulary-editing\">edit</link> a collection, click on "
"the <guilabel>Editor Icon</guilabel> on its right hand side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you'd like to start your own collection of vocabulary, click on "
"<guilabel>Create a New Collection</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also <link linkend=\"open-an-existing-collection\">open a "
"collection</link> if you have it on your computer already but it's not in "
"the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last button on the <guilabel>Start Page</guilabel> offers you to "
"download vocabulary collections made by others. When you've created a file "
"that you'd like to share with others, you can easily upload it from the "
"editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley comes with different themes, you can switch to a different graphical "
"style in the settings. For further information, see <link linkend="
"\"configure-parley\">Configure Parley</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open an existing collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let's suppose your collection is already on your hard disk."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is what the screen will look like the first time you start Parley:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on <guilabel>Open an Existing Collection</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the file selection dialog, navigate to the directory containing the data "
"file, and select it by clicking on it. Depending on your system the file "
"either opens immediately, or you have to click <guilabel>OK</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now, the file is loaded, and you move on to the <guilabel>Practice Setup</"
"guilabel> screen: see the following section for further details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vocabulary Practice"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To start practicing you select a document after starting Parley. If you have "
"it opened in the editor already, just click <guilabel>Practice</guilabel> in "
"the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Practice Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before the actual practice starts, you always get to the Practice Setup "
"page. There are three areas which allow you to choose what to practice:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "The selection of languages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "The selection of the practice mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "The selection of the lessons that also shows your current progress"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left you can select the combination of languages you will practice. "
"If you select for example English to French, you will be shown English words "
"and Parley will ask you to enter the French translations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the language selection you choose the practice mode. "
"<guilabel>Practice Mode</guilabel> determines how the practice will ask you "
"questions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the big part on the right, you see the lessons of the vocabulary "
"collection. You can select which lessons you want to practice with the "
"checkbox in front of the lesson name. The number of words that each lesson "
"contains is shown next to its name. On the right of the name you see your "
"current progress for the lesson."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Practice Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Advanced Practice Configuration</guilabel> allows you to "
"specify more advanced settings that will affect the practice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <link linkend=\"practice-setup\">Practice Setup</link> page you reach "
"the <guilabel>Advanced Practice Configuration</guilabel> with the "
"<guilabel>Configure Practice</guilabel> button in the toolbar. The button "
"with the green icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "Blocking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you plan to practice your vocabulary regularly, you should make sure that "
"the <emphasis>Blocking</emphasis> feature is enabled. The "
"<guilabel>Blocking</guilabel> options are part of the <link linkend="
"\"advanced-practice-configuration\">Advanced Practice Configuration</link>. "
"There you go to the blocking page and tick the checkbox that says "
"<guilabel>Blocking</guilabel>. Now you can even configure the interval in "
"which words that you answered correctly will be repeated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Blocking</emphasis> means that words will not be asked for some "
"period of time after the last practice. This period of time depends on how "
"well you know the word, so that words you don't know yet will be asked more "
"frequently."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thresholds"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thresholds are another way of limiting what you want to practice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can decide to practice only words that you know better or less well than "
"some grade. Or you can select only words that you have practiced a certain "
"number of times."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Practice Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find several more configuration options for the practice in the "
"advanced settings page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "The most important options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Ignore Accents: with this option if you enter a word with <guilabel>e</"
"guilabel> instead of <guilabel>é</guilabel> it will still count as right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Ignore Capitalization: this option allows you to ignore capitalization when "
"you enter words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Images and Sound: if you enable images they will be displayed during the "
"practice, if they are available. Same applies to Sound."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:272
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Article"
msgid "Practice"
msgstr "Article"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "Flash Cards"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After having activated the <guilabel>Flash Card</guilabel> Practice Mode and "
"having clicked on <guilabel>Start Practice</guilabel> the following screen "
"shows up. The Flash Card training mode works just as if you would do it with "
"<quote>real</quote> flash cards. You imagine the result and should you wish "
"some help, you can click on <guilabel>Hint</guilabel> which will start to "
"give you the result one letter at a time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also decide to skip a word for now. When you click <guilabel>Answer "
"Later</guilabel> the word will show up again at a later time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> reveals the solution. At this "
"stage you then have to tell if you knew the answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you did not know it, click <guilabel>I did not know it</guilabel>. If you "
"did remember the answer, click <guilabel>I knew it</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will take you to the next question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left hand side bottom of the screen you have 7 boxes that show how "
"good you know the vocabulary. These 7 boxes correspond to the blocking "
"levels set under <link linkend=\"blocking\"><guilabel>Blocking</guilabel></"
"link> in the <guilabel>Advanced Practice Configuration</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead of clicking <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> you can also use the "
"<keycap>Spacebar</keycap> of your keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:314 index.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can stop practicing anytime by clicking on <guilabel>Stop Practice</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mixed Letters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mixed Letters is a training method that provides you with an immediate help: "
"all letters that are part of the solution are shown mixed up:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Should you wish some help, you can click on <guilabel>Hint</guilabel> which "
"will give you the solution one letter at a time. Of course you can also "
"decide to <guilabel>Answer Later</guilabel> by clicking on that button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To give the answer type it in the blank field below the mixed letters and "
"press the &Enter; key or <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your answer was correct Parley will tell you so and you can press &Enter; "
"again or click on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> to go ahead with the next "
"question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Should you enter a wrong answer, you will be told to <emphasis>try again</"
"emphasis>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't know the answer, just click on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> a "
"second time. Then the following comes up and you are shown the solution. Go "
"ahead with <guilabel>Continue</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:382 index.docbook:434 index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After the solution is revealed, you see a big icon on the right that "
"indicates if your answer will count as right or wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:384 index.docbook:436 index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can overrule how your answer is counted. See <link linkend=\"counting-an-"
"answer-as-right\">Counting an Answer as Right</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multiple Choice"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic selection of the possible answers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <guilabel>Multiple Choice</guilabel> mode you are shown a number of "
"potential answers, of which only one is correct. By clicking on "
"<guilabel>Hint</guilabel> Parley excludes one of the wrong answers so that "
"your choice gets more and more restricted with each further click on "
"<guilabel>Hint</guilabel>. Of course you may also choose to <guilabel>Answer "
"Later</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you made your choice by clicking on what you believe to be correct, "
"Parley shows up with the screen below if the answer was right. Go ahead with "
"the next question by clicking on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your answer instead was wrong, the correct answer will be shown in green "
"and the wrong one in red. Also here you go ahead by clicking on "
"<guilabel>Continue</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you wish to stop practice, just click on the <guilabel>Stop Practice</"
"guilabel> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "With yes/no answers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally Parley automatically proposes one correct and several wrong answers "
"in Multiple Choice mode. For some exercises instead you will have preset "
"answers like yes/no or similar. And for these you have to configure the "
"practice by clicking on <link linkend=\"advanced-practice-configuration"
"\"><guilabel>Configure Practice</guilabel></link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the tab <guilabel>Advanced</guilabel> and you will get something very "
"similar to the following screenshot:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have just <emphasis>two choices</emphasis> like <emphasis>yes/no</"
"emphasis> in the section <guilabel>Multiple Choice</guilabel> set the "
"<guilabel>Number of choices</guilabel> to <guilabel>2</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Written"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you select the option <guilabel>Written</guilabel> to do your practice "
"you are supposed to type in the solution. You can use the button "
"<guilabel>Hint</guilabel> which will start to give you the result one letter "
"at a time. Of course you can also decide to <guilabel>Answer Later</"
"guilabel> by clicking on that button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have entered the solution, click on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> "
"and Parley will show whether your answer was correct. Go ahead by clicking "
"on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Should you give a wrong answer, you may try again several times to find the "
"right answer. If you don't try again, and just click on <guilabel>Continue</"
"guilabel>, the solution will be shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Go ahead practicing by clicking on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel> or stop by "
"clicking on the button <guilabel>Stop Practice</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the solution is revealed, you see a big icon on the right that "
"indicates if your answer will count as right or wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "Counting an Answer as Right"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you see the big checkmark, Parley thinks you were right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you needed more than one attempt to answer correctly, your answer will be "
"counted as wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click the small icon next to the indicator to change how your answer "
"is counted. The big symbol always indicates how the answer is counted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reset Practice to Initial State"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can reset all your practice scores (remove the grades) to the initial "
"state. When being in edit mode select <guilabel>Edit</guilabel> from the "
"menu bar and then <guilabel>Remove Grades</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore you can reset your grades for individual lessons from within the "
"<guilabel>Practice Setup</guilabel> by right clicking on the lesson to reset "
"and choose <guilabel>Remove Grades</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:559
#, no-c-format
msgid "Summary After Practice"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The summary shows up when you finish a learning session. In the big bar on "
"the top it shows you how well you did."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below is a table with all the words you practiced, together with the "
"mistakes you made."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The words with the most mistakes are on top so you can easily see what you "
"do not know yet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "Grammar Practice Modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With Parley you can also learn specific grammar structures, such as the "
"gender of nouns, the comparison forms of adjectives and the conjugation of "
"verbs. Let's look at some examples."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Articles and Gender of Nouns"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the practice mode <guilabel>Gender of Nouns</guilabel> is activated, "
"click on <guilabel>Start Practice</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the case below we use German as language to learn and so you have three "
"genders to choose from: masculine, feminine and neuter. By clicking on "
"<guilabel>Hint</guilabel> one of the wrong answers gets excluded. Of course "
"you can also decide to <guilabel>Answer Later</guilabel> by clicking on that "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should enter the articles for the language in the Editor to see the "
"articles instead of the grammatical gender terms. Also note that this only "
"works, if the gender of the words has been set up properly. See <link "
"linkend=\"word-types\">Word Types</link> for more information how to change "
"the word type to the right gender."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you give the correct answer the following is shown and you go ahead "
"practicing by clicking on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Should you give the wrong answer the following is shown and you go ahead "
"practicing by clicking on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comparison Forms of Adjectives and Adverbs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Practice</guilabel> screen select <guilabel>Comparison "
"Forms</guilabel> and then click on <guilabel>Start Practice</guilabel> to go "
"ahead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This only works when the conjugation forms of the word have been entered in "
"the vocabulary collection. See <link linkend=\"entering-comparison-forms"
"\">Entering Comparison Forms</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The exercise requires you to enter the comparison forms for the term shown. "
"In this case the translation of the English word <emphasis>old</emphasis> to "
"German. The German language has three forms: <emphasis>absolute, "
"comparative</emphasis> and <emphasis>superlative</emphasis>. To go on with "
"the exercise just click on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:670
#, no-c-format
msgid "Conjugations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To practice conjugations choose the <guilabel>Conjugations</guilabel> mode "
"and the tenses you wish to exercise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:673
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the document the conjugation forms of the words have to be entered in "
"order to allow this practice mode to work. See <link linkend=\"entering-"
"inflection-forms\">Entering Inflection Forms</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then click on <guilabel>Start Practice</guilabel>. You are required to enter "
"the correct conjugation forms according to the tense shown. To go ahead "
"click on <guilabel>Continue</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:706
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vocabulary Editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you start using a vocabulary collection or create your own it is "
"helpful to understand the different elements in Parley and configure them "
"accordingly. The next sections will guide you step by step through this "
"process. There are several locations in Parley for settings:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> This is the place for the <quote>General Document Properties</"
"quote>, meaning some information about your vocabulary collection and "
"yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Languages</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> Find here settings around the languages you use"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Practice</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Practice</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> Here are settings how you practice your "
"vocabulary. Depending on what you want to do during the specific learning "
"session you change them on the fly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Parley</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> For more general and display settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid "About the Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entering meta data like a title and your contact info is relevant if you "
"plan to make your collection available for other people. Use "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> to edit the data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:750
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vocabulary Columns"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on what your learning sessions are going to be about it can be "
"relevant to have further Vocabulary Columns show up in your edit section. To "
"choose these columns select <guilabel>View</guilabel> from the Menu bar and "
"then <guilabel>Vocabulary Columns</guilabel>. There you can determine if the "
"columns for <emphasis>Pronunciation, Word Type, Synonym, Antonym, Example, "
"Comment</emphasis> and/or <emphasis>Paraphrase</emphasis> are to be shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid "Languages and Grammar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:768
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set up some grammar details to let Parley help you. Use "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Languages</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> to pull up the grammar dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Articles in English are simply <guilabel>the</guilabel> which is the "
"definite article and <guilabel>a</guilabel> as indefinite article. Most "
"other languages have more articles which can be filled in at the articles "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:772
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For conjugations the personal pronouns should be filled out. Most languages "
"do not have different conjugation forms for he/she/it, in that case, you "
"should <emphasis>not</emphasis> check <guilabel>Male/Female have different "
"conjugations</guilabel>! Simply enter the pronouns for all three forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:776
#, no-c-format
msgid "Personal Pronouns in English"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "Singular"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plural"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:785
#, no-c-format
msgid "1st Person"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:786
#, no-c-format
msgid "<entry>I</entry>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:787
#, no-c-format
msgid "<entry>we</entry>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:790
#, no-c-format
msgid "2nd Person"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:791 index.docbook:792
#, no-c-format
msgid "<entry>you</entry>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:795
#, no-c-format
msgid "3rd Person"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid "he/she/it"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:797
#, no-c-format
msgid "they"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tenses: Depending on the language, you can enter the right tenses which you "
"later want to learn how to conjugate. Examples are: Simple Present, Simple "
"Past, Future I etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:805
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Btw. by clicking on the <guilabel>Add Language</guilabel> button you can add "
"an additional language to your collection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:807
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let's Have a Closer Look at Spanish"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:808
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab the basic language settings, like "
"here"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:811
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Language</guilabel> = Spanish"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:813
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Name</guilabel> = Spanish"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:815
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Keyboard layout</guilabel> = de (for German)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:818
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can leave <guilabel>Keyboard layout</guilabel> empty if you are not sure "
"about what you are using. Parley will then simply take the standard layout "
"of your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's have a look at the <guilabel>Articles</guilabel> tab: Spanish knows "
"only male and female nouns, therefore the field <guilabel>Neutral</guilabel> "
"remains empty."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:848
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Spanish <guilabel>Personal Pronouns</guilabel> have multiple forms for 3rd "
"person singular and 1st, 2nd and 3rd person plural. To remain consistent, "
"the possibilities should be entered with a <guilabel>/</guilabel> between "
"the two forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:863
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under <guilabel>Tenses</guilabel> you will find the various tenses that are "
"available for a verb form. You can add to the tenses that are already there "
"by clicking on <guilabel>New</guilabel>, modify with <guilabel>Modify</"
"guilabel> or in case something does not actually exist simply "
"<guilabel>Delete</guilabel> the tense after having it selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:881
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lessons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:882
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left you have a list of lessons. If you started a new collection, "
"this list might be empty except for one lesson that was created by default "
"for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you cannot see the list of lessons, you might have to enable it in the "
"View menu - <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Lessons</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The check boxes in front of the lesson name show which lessons are currently "
"included in your practice. The number next to it is the number of words in "
"the lesson."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:888
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Lesson"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Add a new lesson: Select where this lesson belongs to, for example the "
"collection <guilabel>My Spanish Lessons</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:904
#, no-c-format
msgid "In the Lesson menu, select <guilabel>New Lesson</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please make sure to select the right point in the tree structure of lessons "
"before selecting <guilabel>New Lesson</guilabel>. In our case, wanting a "
"<emphasis>Sub-Lesson</emphasis> of <guilabel>Collection: My Spanish Lessons</"
"guilabel> it is exactly that one that needs to be selected before going "
"ahead with <guilabel>New Lesson</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving, Renaming and Deleting Lessons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the name of a lesson, double click it, or right click on the "
"lesson and choose <guilabel>Rename Lesson</guilabel>. You can also delete it "
"this way (but you'll lose its contents also then)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't like the arrangement of lessons, you can move a lesson with the "
"mouse. You can drag it onto another lesson, then it will become a child of "
"that lesson."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid "Splitting a Lesson"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:929
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your lessons grow too big, you can choose to split them up to make "
"learning easier in small units. 20 words for a lesson is probably a good "
"size. Right click a lesson, or use <menuchoice><guimenu>Lesson</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Split Lesson into Smaller Lessons</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> and the lesson will be separated into child lessons. You can "
"choose to randomize the words that are put into the new lessons before "
"assigning them, or to keep them in order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:932
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is Shown in the Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:933
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley shows always the words of the lesson that you have currently "
"selected. You can enable to see the words in sub-lessons contained in this "
"lesson also. Use <menuchoice><guimenu>Lesson</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show "
"Entries from Child Lessons</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to enable this. That "
"way, you can browse all words by selecting the document lesson at the very "
"top."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:937
#, no-c-format
msgid "Word Types"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:938
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parley lets you associate word types with the words. Word types are for "
"example: Nouns, Verbs, Adjectives and Adverbs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:940
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to work with word types, enable the word type tool: "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Word Types</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can categorize the word types just like lessons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to see all words of a certain type - e.g. all nouns, simply "
"select the noun category, and you will see only nouns in the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to set the word type, is to drag and drop a word onto its "
"type. You can even do this with multiple words at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:953
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding New Vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <guilabel>Add New Entry</guilabel> in the toolbar to add new words. You "
"can start typing the word in the first language right away. By default "
"Parley lets you enter another word when you press &Enter; in the last row, "
"so you don't have to keep using the <guilabel>Add</guilabel> button. After "
"entering the first word, press &Tab; to go to the next language."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing Words"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:958
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to replace a word, select its entry and start typing. To change "
"the word instead, double click the entry and you can change the contents of "
"the cell without losing the old word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:960
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press &Tab; to go to the next word while staying in editing mode. &Enter; "
"leaves this mode. You can use the arrow keys to move around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:964
#, no-c-format
msgid "Synonyms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:965
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Synonyms are hard to set up and do not always work really well. Here is how "
"you set them up in any case:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:968
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Synonyms</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> to see the synonyms tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select first word (A) you want to make synonyms, then click on the second "
"word (B)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:972
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button in the synonym tool changes it's text to <guilabel>A and B are "
"synonyms</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The words will now be shown as connected in the synonym tool and can be "
"recognized as synonyms in the practice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding Images"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:979
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First show the image tool by selecting <guilabel>View</guilabel> in the menu "
"bar and then clicking on <guilabel>Image</guilabel>. The checkbox in front "
"of <guilabel>Image</guilabel> will then be activated. This will show up the "
"picture section on the right hand side of the Parley screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add an image to a word make sure the word is highlighted. In the image "
"section on the right hand side click on the <emphasis>Folder icon</emphasis> "
"and choose the picture you wish to associate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:997
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding Sound"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:998
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First show the sound tool by selecting <guilabel>View</guilabel> in the menu "
"bar and then clicking on <guilabel>Sound</guilabel>. This will show up the "
"sound section on the right hand side of the Parley screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1000
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a sound to a word make sure the word is highlighted. In the sound "
"section on the right hand side click on the <emphasis>Folder icon</emphasis> "
"and choose the sound you wish to associate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1016
#, no-c-format
msgid "Entering Comparison Forms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1017
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to enter comparison forms, make sure the comparison forms tool is "
"enabled. You open it with the menu: <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Comparison Forms</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid "First select a word that is an adjective or adverb."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1034
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guilabel>Adjective</guilabel> or <guilabel>Adverb</guilabel> "
"button in the comparison forms tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1049
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the comparison forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1064
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can use the <link linkend=\"comparison-forms-of-adjectives-and-"
"adverbs\">Comparison Forms Practice</link> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid "Entering Inflection Forms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1068
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to enter inflection forms, make sure the inflection forms tool is "
"enabled. You open it with the menu: <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Inflection (verbs, adjectives, nouns)</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1070
#, no-c-format
msgid "First select a word that is a verb."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1085
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the <guilabel>Verb</guilabel> button in the inflections tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After selecting the right tense in the tense selection box, enter the "
"conjugation forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tenses can be configured for each language: <link linkend=\"languages-"
"and-grammar\">Languages and Grammar</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can use the <link linkend=\"conjugations\">Conjugations Practice</"
"link> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <guibutton>Noun</guibutton> or <guibutton>Adjective</guibutton> "
"button to add declension forms to your vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating New Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section we will describe how to create new files and this not only "
"with the usual vocabulary learning part, but also for grammar exercises, "
"mathematics etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1111
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Collection: Vocabulary English-German"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section we describe how you can create a vocabulary training file "
"including pictures and sound. In a second stage we will also add adjectives "
"and verbs. This is a very complete example and therefore quite long. "
"Eventually you will not need all points for your project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since we wish to add sound-files and pictures, we should make sure that "
"these will all be in one folder which for convenience is being called "
"<emphasis>eng-deu</emphasis>. Our data file we create with Parley will be "
"saved in the same folder. This will help a lot when you decide to share your "
"work with others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid "So this is what we have in terms of sound files and pictures:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's start from the <guilabel>Start Page</guilabel> which is shown once you "
"launch Parley:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on the button <guilabel>Create a New Collection</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>General Document Properties</guilabel> page shows up which is "
"being filled as follows (just adapt to what your file is about):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel>. The following screen asks you to set "
"up the language details. Here we don't want to change anything and therefore "
"we just click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As a first step, let's create the vocabulary part. We will think about the "
"addition of the sound files and pictures in a second stage. This is what the "
"lesson looks like:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before we do anything else, let's save the file to the folder with the "
"pictures and sound-files. Click on the <guilabel>Save</guilabel> icon and "
"select the folder using the navigation. In this example we will call the "
"file <guilabel>Trainer eng-deu</guilabel> - once you entered the name just "
"click on save."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you now check your folder where the sound-files and pictures are, you "
"will also find the file <guilabel>Trainer eng-deu.kvtml</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's have a short look at the words we want to add: <emphasis>apple, bird, "
"cat, cherry, cow, orange, pear, snake, strawberry</emphasis>. We have "
"animals and fruit and therefore we decide to create two lessons that are "
"called: <guilabel>Animals</guilabel> and <guilabel>Fruit</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We now rename <guilabel>Lesson 1</guilabel> to <guilabel>Animals</guilabel> "
"and then we add a lesson called <guilabel>Fruit</guilabel>. Right-click on "
"<guilabel>Lesson 1</guilabel> and choose <guilabel>Rename Lesson</guilabel> "
"from the options shown. Now <guilabel>Lesson 1</guilabel> is highlighted and "
"you can simply overwrite it by typing in <guilabel>Animals</guilabel>. When "
"done, hit the &Enter; key. Now right-click on <guilabel>Collection: "
"Vocabulary trainer E...</guilabel> which is the root of the lesson tree and "
"choose <guilabel>New Lesson</guilabel> from the options shown. In the new "
"field write <guilabel>Fruit</guilabel> and hit the &Enter; key again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, let's insert the animals. Please click on the lesson "
"<guilabel>Animals</guilabel> and you will get an empty table you can fill "
"in. Click with your mouse in the first field, and insert the source terms. "
"Then, insert the target terms in the second column. Once you've inserted all "
"4 English animal names with their German translation the screen looks like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In our case we want only 4 entries in the animals lesson. There are many "
"empty lines that should be deleted. To do this click on the first empty "
"field, and keep the &Shift; key pressed while clicking on the last empty "
"field. All lines to be deleted will be highlighted. Then, press the "
"<keycap>Del</keycap> key and confirm the question <emphasis>Do you really "
"want to delete the selected entries?</emphasis> by clicking on the "
"<guilabel>Delete</guilabel> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let's add the fruit terminology. Just click on the lesson named "
"<guilabel>Fruit</guilabel>. This second lesson is completely empty. Since we "
"have five fruit terms we need to add five lines. Therefore, press the "
"<keycap>Ins</keycap> key five times, and then, just like before, we add our "
"terminology."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Don't forget to save every now and then ..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A click on the root of our lesson tree <guilabel>Collection: Vocabulary "
"trainer E...</guilabel> and Parley will show us all entries that are present "
"in the two lessons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Time to add sound and images. First of all we need to activate the Image and "
"Sound views. From the menu bar select <guilabel>View</guilabel> and there "
"click on <guilabel>Image</guilabel> and then <guilabel>Sound</guilabel>. "
"Once these options are activated, two new sections are shown on the right "
"hand side of the Parley editing screen: <emphasis>Image</emphasis> and "
"<emphasis>Sound</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the English word <emphasis>apple</emphasis> by clicking on it. It is "
"highlighted, so let's add the picture. In the image section on the right "
"hand side click on the <guilabel>Folder</guilabel> icon and choose the "
"picture you wish to associate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add the pronunciation for the English apple, do the same in the Sound "
"section, selecting the relevant sound file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking on the <guilabel>Play</guilabel> button in the sound tool you "
"can listen to the pronunciation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1258
#, no-c-format
msgid "The screen will then look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then click on the German translation <guilabel>Apfel</guilabel>. The field "
"is now highlighted to indicate the selection. You will note the picture with "
"the apple is associated also to the German term. In the sound section select "
"the pronunciation, just like before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Just go ahead like this for all terms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Time to add adjectives and verbs as lessons to our project. So just do as "
"before with the lesson <emphasis>Fruit</emphasis> and create two new "
"lessons: <emphasis>Adjectives</emphasis> and <emphasis>Verbs</emphasis>. "
"Let's assume we will add <emphasis>big, small, old, young, narrow</emphasis> "
"in the adjective lesson and <emphasis>to go, to come, to buy, to drink, to "
"eat</emphasis> in the verb lesson."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following shows a screenshot with all inserted terminology. Now, words "
"are mixed and it would be nice to see what is a <emphasis>noun, adjective</"
"emphasis> or <emphasis>verb</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As the next step we are going to show the <guilabel>Word Type</guilabel>. "
"Select <guilabel>View</guilabel> in the menu bar and then select "
"<guilabel>Vocabulary Columns</guilabel>. We activate <guilabel>Word Type</"
"guilabel> for <emphasis>English</emphasis> and <emphasis>German</emphasis> "
"by clicking on the checkbox in front of <guilabel>Word Type</guilabel>. Then "
"click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel> to accept the changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking on the fields in the column <guilabel>Word Type</guilabel> you "
"can select the word type and for those languages where nouns have a gender "
"you can also select the <emphasis>Noun/Gender</emphasis> combination. "
"Alternatively start to type the first characters of a word type to select "
"it. Below the <guilabel>Word Type</guilabel> column with part of the "
"selections already done."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once we have specified all the word types, we will first consider "
"<emphasis>Adjectives</emphasis>, adding <guilabel>Comparison Forms</"
"guilabel> to them. So let's move to the <emphasis>Adjectives</emphasis> "
"lesson only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To show the <guilabel>Comparison Forms</guilabel> on the right hand side of "
"the screen, select the <guilabel>View</guilabel> in the menu bar and "
"activate the <guilabel>Comparison Forms</guilabel> checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Edit the <guilabel>Comparison Forms</guilabel> by adding "
"<guilabel>Comparative</guilabel> and <guilabel>Superlative</guilabel> to the "
"single adjectives. First, click on the adjective for which you wish to add "
"the comparison forms, in our case <emphasis>big</emphasis>, and add "
"<emphasis>bigger</emphasis> and <emphasis>biggest</emphasis>. Then, continue "
"with the next adjective to complete, until all comparison forms have been "
"entered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1382
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, let's consider the <guilabel>Conjugation</guilabel> form of the "
"<guilabel>Verbs</guilabel>. Select the <guilabel>Verbs</guilabel> lesson and "
"then activate the conjugation section on the right hand side by selecting "
"<guilabel>View</guilabel> from the menu bar and activating "
"<guilabel>Conjugation</guilabel>. As an example we edit the present tense "
"(<guilabel>Präsens</guilabel>) form of <emphasis>gehen</emphasis>. Please "
"first select <guilabel>Präsens</guilabel> from the drop down menu and then "
"add the verb forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1397
#, no-c-format
msgid "This needs to be done for all verbs, and in all possible tenses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you are done you can start to practice by clicking on the <link linkend="
"\"vocabulary-practice\"><guilabel>Practice</guilabel></link> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1402
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Collection: Single Names and Collective Names"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This exercise was created for the 3rd class of an Italian primary school. "
"Pupils are supposed to connect single names with collective names, such as "
"<emphasis>tree</emphasis> → <emphasis>woods</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start Parley you get the start page, eventually also listing some "
"previously used files (that you cannot see here)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on <guilabel>Create a New Collection</guilabel> and the following "
"screen with empty or partly filled fields will show up:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fill in the title, here <guilabel>nomi singoli e collettivi</guilabel>, your "
"name, e-mail address, in the <guilabel>Comment</guilabel> section you can "
"write down a more detailed description, select your category and license. "
"Then there we have something special: instead of indicating the first and "
"second language, like it normally would happen, we added <emphasis>nome "
"singolo</emphasis> (single name) and <emphasis>nome collettivo</emphasis> "
"(collective name). <guilabel>Setup Grammar Details</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Download Grammar</guilabel> are not needed here. In the screenshot "
"they are still activated - please deactivate them by just clicking on the "
"checkboxes. When you are done, please click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Languages</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> and the <guilabel>Properties for nome singolo</"
"guilabel> page comes up and here you see it already with the necessary "
"changes made:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left hand side you can see where the data you are adding belongs to. "
"<emphasis>nome singolo</emphasis>. Choose the language, here "
"<emphasis>Italian</emphasis> and insert <emphasis>nome singolo</emphasis> in "
"the following editable field. Then click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now the <guilabel>Properties for nome collettivo</guilabel> page is shown:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Like before: choose <guilabel>Italian</guilabel> as language and insert "
"<emphasis>nome collettivo</emphasis> and click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1471
#, no-c-format
msgid "And now you can start to edit:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just insert the <emphasis>nome singolo</emphasis> (single name) in the first "
"column and the corresponding <emphasis>nome collettivo</emphasis> "
"(collective name) in the second column."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1501
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the number of available fields is not enough, just right-click anywhere "
"on the edit section and choose <guilabel>Add New Entry</guilabel>. Don't "
"forget to save your file every now and then. When you have finished adding "
"all entries you will want to see if Practice mode works fine. Well just "
"click on the <guilabel>Practice</guilabel> button right above the edit "
"section and the page with the practice settings comes up:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1516
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this case <guilabel>Multiple Choice</guilabel> is a good option, but also "
"<guilabel>Written</guilabel> will do fine. After choosing the Practice Mode "
"just click on <guilabel>Start Practice</guilabel> and have fun."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1520
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Additional Collections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1521
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are on the <guilabel>Start Page</guilabel> you have the possibility "
"to install collections directly from the server, provided you are online. "
"Just click on <guilabel>Download New Collections</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1536
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A window with many interesting collections opens. Just select what you find "
"most interesting and click on <guilabel>Install</guilabel>. Then open the "
"file to practice or edit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1552
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Parley"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can configure the appearance of Parley from the <guilabel>Start Page</"
"guilabel> or from within the <guilabel>Edit section</guilabel>. Select "
"<guilabel>Settings</guilabel> from the menu bar and then <guilabel>Configure "
"Parley</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1568
#, no-c-format
msgid "Theme Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration opens with the <guilabel>Theme</guilabel> section. This is "
"the place where you can choose how Parley should greet you when launching "
"it: an elegant <guilabel>Grey</guilabel> version, the all time busy "
"<guilabel>Bees</guilabel> or the <guilabel>Fluffy Bunny</guilabel> for all "
"those who love pink. Note that it could well be that <guilabel>Fluffy Bunny</"
"guilabel> is not in your version: if you want it, read the following section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you selected your preferred theme, click on <guilabel>OK</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Screenshots of the <guilabel>Bees</guilabel> and <guilabel>Fluffy Bunny</"
"guilabel> themes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And if these are not enough: you can click on <guilabel>Get New Themes</"
"guilabel> to find more themes. Over time we hope that more and more themes "
"come along. If you know how to create SVG graphics (for example with <ulink "
"url=\"http://inkscape.org\"><application>Inkscape</application></ulink>), "
"you can create your own theme and share it with the world."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additional themes can be found on <ulink url=\"http://kde-look.org/index.php?"
"xcontentmode=85\">kde-look.org </ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1619
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab gives you some options regarding the "
"behavior of Parley."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1622
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open/Save options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Always load the last opened collection on start</guilabel> will "
"immediately take you back to the vocabulary you were learning. Often you "
"will use this together with the second option <guilabel>Save vocabularies "
"automatically on close and quit</guilabel> because it's just handy not to "
"have always answer the same question if changes (including learning results) "
"should be changed or not. The option <guilabel>Create a backup every ... "
"minutes</guilabel> can be very handy to help you save your work frequently. "
"One less thing to think about."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes the import and/or export of text (CSV) files can be very handy and "
"there you need the proper separator to elaborate data afterwards or to be "
"able to read the data you got from somewhere else. Parley allows you to "
"choose among various separators to make sure you can re-use your data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1628
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing option"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1629
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can determine whether Parley automatically appends new rows while "
"you are editing your vocabulary collection. This can be useful if you want "
"to add many entries, before then splitting them up into various lessons. On "
"the other hand, it can be good to have this option off if you want to work "
"by creating lessons with a set maximum number of entries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1646
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>View Settings</guilabel> allows you to change font and size "
"for the pronunciation symbols, and you can choose the <guilabel>Grade "
"Colors</guilabel> you like best."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1665
#, no-c-format
msgid "Parley on Windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is possible to install Parley together with other <ulink url=\"http://edu."
"kde.org\">Educational software</ulink> on Windows systems. For further info "
"please visit <ulink url=\"http://windows.kde.org\">this page</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1668
#, no-c-format
msgid "The steps to be followed in short:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1670
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Download the installer <ulink url=\"http://windows.kde.org/download.php"
"\">here</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then follow the installation procedure like for any other Windows software - "
"screenshots are <ulink url=\"http://www.winkde.org/pub/kde/ports/win32/"
"installer/manual/\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1674
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you come to the <guilabel>Package selection screen</guilabel>, select "
"the language(s) you wish the software to be available in <emphasis>and</"
"emphasis> the package - in this case <guilabel>kdeedu</guilabel>. If you "
"don't select any language you will automatically get English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then finish the installation process by clicking on next, following the "
"coming screens just like you normally do with other windows software."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1678
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please note that the Parley team does not deal with the Windows-Installer "
"and therefore we cannot easily answer your questions. Should you have "
"difficulties, please contact the KDE-Windows team directly. You can do so by "
"subscribing to the mailing list <ulink url=\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/"
"listinfo/kde-windows\">here</ulink> or join them on IRC at irc://freenode."
"net Channel: #kde-windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1681
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notes For Advanced Users"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1696
#, no-c-format
msgid "Upload and Share Collections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1697
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can upload your files and share them with others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1699
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <guimenuitem>Upload Vocabulary Document</guimenuitem> from the file menu "
"in the Editor within Parley."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If that does not work, you can also visit <ulink url=\"http://kde-files.org/?"
"xcontentmode=687\">kde-files.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1703
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In either case the files will show up in the <guilabel>Download New "
"Collections</guilabel> dialog on the <guilabel>Start Page</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1706
#, no-c-format
msgid "File format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are interested in the file formats that Parley can read and stores "
"the vocabulary collections in, visit:"
msgstr ""

